Today is Friday evening.
I want some special spices for tomorrow's cooking.
I take my bicycle out.
The streets shine after the rain.
I ring the bicycle bell and go forward slowly.
I stop near a familiar grocery shop.
I park the bicycle outside the shop and go inside.
The shop owner is standing at the counter.
"Hello Kaka," I say to him with a smile.
"Hello Madam, what can I give you today?" Kaka asks.
I look at my list.
"Give me turmeric, red chili powder, and cumin," I tell him.
Kaka puts all those spices in a bag.
"Do you want anything else?" he asks.
"Yes, give me a packet of garam masala too," I say.
He gives me the bag and says, "That is eighty rupees."
I give him the money.
I put the bag in the bicycle basket.
A nice fragrance of the spices is coming.
Thinking about tomorrow's special meal, I ride back home.
